% What lesson 21's taint analysis should report.
% A fact must be derived; `:- fact.` must never be, and may use variables.
%
%   python3 diagnose.py programs/taint.dl --expect programs/taint.expect
%   python3 mutation.py programs/taint.dl --expect programs/taint.expect

flow(p, q).                      % call c1 passes q to id's parameter
flow(p, lit).                    % call c2 passes a literal
flow(t, p).                      % ...and id returns its parameter
tainted(t).
finding(sink1, t).               % user input reaches the query
:- finding(sink3, safe).         % the sanitizer's result is clean
:- tainted(safe).
